<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns all secondary auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned</p>
<p>all seven auctions whereby it sought to drain 9.490 billion</p>
<p>pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The auctions were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>	750 million  11 days   26.40 pct</p>
<p>	750 million  10 days   26.44 pct</p>
<p>    1.500 bln   9 days   27.23 pct</p>
<p>    2.800 bln   8 days   28.70 pct</p>
<p>    2.200 bln   7 days   28.00 pct</p>
<p>    1.200 bln   3 days   27.50 pct</p>
<p>	290 million   1 day    26.50 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
